From: System Electronics
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: report a failed phy_power_on

cdns_dsi_hs_init() ignored the return value of phy_power_on(). With the
guard added in 0013, a power_on in the wrong state returns -EINVAL, and
the link bring-up would carry on as if the PHY were up.

The phy core already logs "phy poweron failed" against the phy device.
This adds the line on the DSI side, where the bring-up continues
regardless, so the two can be read together.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
@@ -715,7 +715,7 @@
 {
 	struct cdns_dsi_output *output = &dsi->output;
 	u32 status, stale;
-	int i;
+	int i, ret;
 	
 	if (dsi->phy_initialized)
 		return;
@@ -731,7 +731,9 @@
 	phy_init(dsi->dphy);
 	phy_set_mode(dsi->dphy, PHY_MODE_MIPI_DPHY);
 	phy_configure(dsi->dphy, &output->phy_opts);
-	phy_power_on(dsi->dphy);
+	ret = phy_power_on(dsi->dphy);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(dsi->base.dev, "phy_power_on failed: %d\n", ret);
 
 	/* Activate the PLL and wait until it's locked. */
 	stale = PLL_LOCKED | CLK_LANE_RDY;
